{"approved":false,"back_sample":null,"beam_size":2,"checks":{"no_residual_markers":true,"nonempty":true,"not_truncated":true,"protected_values":true,"translated":true},"context":"rlc-circuit-calculator UI copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer","detected_language":"it","format":"usefulverse-background-draft-v1","key":"rlc-circuit-calculator.copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer","keys":["rlc-circuit-calculator.copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer"],"locale":"it","model":"google/madlad400-3b-mt","raw_translation":"Per il modello in serie, Q = ω₀L/R e la larghezza di banda è R/(ZXQPH0000QXZπL). Per il modello in parallelo, Q = R/(ω₀L) e la larghezza di banda è ZXQPH0001QXZ/(ZXQPH0002QXZπRC).","record_id":"abf878a032e8019c187de1bb12e50147df089dbab8185a2db901c87571ec69fc","revision":"fa184c675da0b5c9e1c8694fccd4e12e2d422094","run_id":"40843674935","seconds":1.9833597438750417,"source":"For the series model, Q = ω₀L/R and bandwidth is R/(2πL). For the parallel model, Q = R/(ω₀L) and bandwidth is 1/(2πRC). These are ideal single-resonance relationships.","source_commit":"e1f72394198c1a94fce448ea14cd79b496701273","source_hash":"d929113d31b49cd67fa0b70f4d3ec5403c3e4e89c98b4fcab359fb6074436c8a","status":"machine-draft","translation":"Per il modello in serie, Q = ω₀L/R e la larghezza di banda è R/(2πL). Per il modello in parallelo, Q = R/(ω₀L) e la larghezza di banda è 1/(2πRC).","truncated":false,"warnings":[]}
